+## Evidence observed
+
+- evidence/hg-lnw.9/tier3-final-rebased.log: e2e_private_herdr 42 passed, adopt_private_herdr 8 passed. tier3-run2-summary.log is an earlier run with two e2e failures; the failing assertion at e2e line 3831 no longer exists at head.
+- evidence/hg-lnw.23/tier3-adopted-unlabelled-rebased.log: the four hg-lnw.9 e2e scenarios pass after the agent-name fix.
+- evidence/hg-lnw.8 and hg-lnw.22 tier5 logs: threads_real 9 passed with tier 5 on. In the full-suite logs threads_real runs 4 tests in 0.01 s, so tier 5 was off there.
+- evidence/hg-lnw.9/late-rebind-pinned-order.log: the late order was exercised once. The fresh check-in was refused on the held seat (`TargetUnresolved`), and one prompt bound the seat afterwards.
+- Teardown: `E2e::drop` sends SIGCONT and then SIGKILL to the daemon (after an argv check) and reaps the root. `reap_root` falls back to SIGKILL, so the SIGSTOP freeze in the late-rebind test cannot leak a stopped process on panic.
+- I re-ran no tests. The verdict rests on reading the code and the committed logs.
+
+## Findings
+
+- `late_rebind_binds_the_fresh_agent_at_its_next_prompt` does not pin the order it is named for. The `late` branch, where the check-in is refused on the held seat and the rebind opens no binding, is asserted only when the race goes that way. Otherwise the test passes through the early order. One committed run shows the late order; a regression in the late path could still pass on a lucky run.
+- `operator_rebind_resurrects_and_places` builds the remedy argv by hand instead of parsing `clone_status::operator_rebind_remedy`. Today they agree (`herdr-threads human seat rebind SEAT --pane PANE --operator`), but no test ties graph's printed remedy to what real threads accepts. This is the follow-up the hg-lnw.21 report noted.
+- Several tier-3 tests wait out the 90 s grace two or three times (`PAST_GRACE` = 200 s), so e2e_private_herdr takes about 15 min. That is the spec's accepted bounded wait, not a defect, but it raises the cost of running tier 3.
+
+## Verdict
+ready
